<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madan Gopal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. <a href="/years/1556">1556</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Madan Gopal was the founder of Sonepur State in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>. A younger son of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chauhan">Chauhan</a> ruling house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patna">Patna</a> (Patnagarh), he received in 1556 the territory around the confluence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahanadi">Mahanadi</a> and Tel rivers, and his descendants ruled Sonepur as a separate Chauhan line until the princely state merged with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1948.</p></div>
